// Consent component - explicit terms / GDPR consent checkbox.
// Distinct from a generic checkbox so consent semantics are explicit in stored results.
// Submitted/stored value is simply 'true'; consent metadata (timestamp, terms version) is out of scope (issue #158).
// The linked terms target MUST be readable by anonymous visitors (guest permissions),
// otherwise the link will 404 for non-authenticated users.
// fmdbmix:booleanField makes the field a conditional-logic source (is true / is false),
// e.g. to reveal fields only once consent is given.
[fmdbext:consent] > jnt:content, fmdbmix:element, fmdbmix:profileMappableField, fmdbmix:booleanField, fmdbmix:validationMessages
 - helpText (string, richtext[ckeditor.toolbar='FormidableHelp',ckeditor.customConfig='$context/modules/formidable-engine/javascript/ckeditor/helpTextConfig.js']) i18n indexed=no
 // Plain text: the statement renders inside the checkbox <label>, whose content
 // model is phrasing-only; the terms link has its own dedicated properties.
 - statement (string,textarea) i18n indexed=no mandatory
 - termsTarget (weakreference) indexed=no < 'jnt:page', 'jnt:file'
 - termsLinkLabel (string) i18n indexed=no
 - required (boolean) = true autocreated
